<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet  xml:id="goal" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
        <title>Optimization Problems</title>
      <exercise>
		<statement>
        <p>
          A rectangular beam is to be cut from a cylindrical log of
          radius 30 cm. The <em>strength</em>, <m>S</m> of the beam is
          given by the formula <md>
          S = kwh^2,
          </md> where <m>w</m> is the width of the beam,
          <m>h</m> is the height, and <m>k</m> is a positive constant.
          Find the dimensions that should be used to create the beam of
          greatest strength.
        </p>
      	</statement>
	</exercise>
      <exercise>
		<statement>
        <p>
          A rectangular box with a square bottom and closed top is to be
          made from two materials. The material for the bottom and sides
          costs $0.005 per square centimeter and the material for the
          top costs $0.007 per square centimeter. If you are willing to
          spend $15 on the box, what is the largest volume it can
          contain?
        </p>
      	</statement>
	</exercise>
      <exercise>
		<statement>
        <p>
          A wire of length 20<nbsp/>cm is to be cut into two pieces; one
          is to be bent into the shape of a square, the other bent into
          the shape of an equilateral triangle. What is the largest
          combined area the two shapes can enclose? What is the
          smallest?
        </p>
      	</statement>
	</exercise>
      <exercise>
		<introduction>
        <p>
          A soup can in the shape of a right circular cylinder is to be
          made from two materials. The material for the <q>sides</q>
          costs $0.0015 per square centimeter and the material for the
          two <q>lids</q> costs $0.0027 per square centimeter. The can
          must have a volume of 250 cubic centimeters. Find the
          dimensions of the can which minimize the cost of the can. Some
          suggestions:
        </p>
</introduction>

            <task>
		<statement>
              <p>
                Draw the can and label the dimensions.
              </p>
      </statement>
            	</task>
            <task>
		<statement>
              <p>
                Find the cost of the lids and the cost of the sides
                <ndash/> surface area is key here.
              </p>
            	</statement>
	</task>
            <task>
		<statement>
              <p>
                Determine a total cost function as a function of one
                variable.
              </p>
            	</statement>
	</task>
            <task>
		<statement>
              <p>
                Minimize the total cost.
              </p>
            	</statement>
	</task>
	</exercise>
      <exercise>
		<statement>
        <p>
          According to postal regulations, the girth plus the length of
          a parcel sent by mail may not exceed 108 in. What is the
          largest possible volume of a rectangular parcel with a square
          end that can be sent by mail? (Note: Girth is the perimeter of
          the square end.)
        </p>
      	</statement>
	</exercise>
</worksheet>
